  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "26105556",
      "title": "Type Inference",
      "lectureOrder": 754,
      "videoOrder": 694,
      "sourceHash": "c4fdcda23fc84743cf9a0cc0d0bae506489cbe9393b6be3f076f35a145a8c338",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 4.8,
          "en": "Instructor: Now that we learned about those base types,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.8,
          "end": 8.43,
          "en": "before I'll dive into functions and parameters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.43,
          "end": 11.49,
          "en": "I want to talk about type inference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.49,
          "end": 14.34,
          "en": "In all those examples which are listed here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.34,
          "end": 18.42,
          "en": "I always declared a variable with a type assigned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.42,
          "end": 22.59,
          "en": "And then in a second step, I set a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.59,
          "end": 26.31,
          "en": "Now, often in programming, you do that in one step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.31,
          "end": 28.5,
          "en": "You create a variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.5,
          "end": 31.983,
          "en": "and you then also immediately assign an initial value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.94,
          "end": 36.48,
          "en": "So therefore, here, let's talk about type inference,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.48,
          "end": 38.94,
          "en": "and let me show you what that is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.94,
          "end": 41.34,
          "en": "Let's say we have another variable down there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.34,
          "end": 42.87,
          "en": "the course variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.87,
          "end": 45.24,
          "en": "And in that course variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.24,
          "end": 47.49,
          "en": "I want to store the name of a course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.49,
          "end": 50.82,
          "en": "like \"React - The Complete Guide.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.82,
          "end": 52.32,
          "en": "Like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.32,
          "end": 55.05,
          "en": "Now, if I create this variable like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.05,
          "end": 58.05,
          "en": "and thereafter I try to store a number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.05,
          "end": 60.366,
          "en": "for example, the course id,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.366,
          "end": 63.12,
          "en": "then you will see that I get an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.12,
          "end": 66.57300000000001,
          "en": "because the type number is not assignable to type string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.47,
          "end": 70.38,
          "en": "But why am I getting this error?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.38,
          "end": 73.95,
          "en": "After all, I don't define a type anywhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.95,
          "end": 77.91,
          "en": "Well, here TypeScript used its powerful feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.91,
          "end": 80.16,
          "en": "of type inference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.16,
          "end": 84.03,
          "en": "By default, TypeScript tries to infer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.03,
          "end": 86.22,
          "en": "as many types as possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.22,
          "end": 90.36,
          "en": "So it tries to know which types are used where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.36,
          "end": 94.08,
          "en": "without you explicitly stating those types,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.08,
          "end": 96.753,
          "en": "which means that you need to write less code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.62,
          "end": 102,
          "en": "I could also set my type here as we learned it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102,
          "end": 105.57,
          "en": "That would not be wrong, but it's redundant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.57,
          "end": 108.18,
          "en": "Because if you immediately initialize",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.18,
          "end": 110.1,
          "en": "this variable with a type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.1,
          "end": 113.4,
          "en": "TypeScript will look at the value type here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.4,
          "end": 117.45,
          "en": "So it will see that we stored a string in that variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.45,
          "end": 120.21,
          "en": "And it will then use that value type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.21,
          "end": 123.96,
          "en": "as an inferred type for this variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.96,
          "end": 128.34,
          "en": "And if you then try to assign a different type thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.34,
          "end": 132.48,
          "en": "you'll get an error because of type inference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.48,
          "end": 136.2,
          "en": "And it is considered a good practice and a good idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.2,
          "end": 139.32,
          "en": "to embrace that type inference feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.32,
          "end": 144.32,
          "en": "so to not unnecessarily specify the type in addition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.32999999999998,
          "end": 145.44,
          "en": "You can do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.44,
          "end": 148.11,
          "en": "You can explicitly state the type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.11,
          "end": 149.57999999999998,
          "en": "but it's really redundant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.57999999999998,
          "end": 152.1,
          "en": "It just means more work from your side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.1,
          "end": 154.17000000000002,
          "en": "And therefore, you should not do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.17000000000002,
          "end": 157.26,
          "en": "You should instead stick to that type inference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.26,
          "end": 160.26,
          "en": "and use it whenever possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.26,
          "end": 163.35,
          "en": "And that's another super important feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.35,
          "end": 165.303,
          "en": "which I wanted to highlight here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
